    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain unobstructed at all times could significantly improve emergency responder approach and egress, particularly given the presence of multiple structures on the property. Posting visible address markers near the primary access point and along the internal drive aisle may assist responders in navigating between the main building, secondary building, and detached structure more efficiently. Preserving adequate turning and staging space within the vehicle parking area or open green space would support apparatus positioning and operational deployment. Where dense vegetation borders the driveway or internal drive aisle, maintaining clearance along those travel corridors could improve responder movement and visibility throughout the property."
